Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.50,0:00:09.50,TitleJa,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,575)}秋の午後の縁側
Dialogue: 2,0:00:11.52,0:01:58.00,Header,,0,0,0,,H006  •  知覚動詞・使役動詞 ＋ O ＋ 原形不定詞
Dialogue: 2,0:00:11.52,0:00:14.52,English,,0,0,0,,It was an autumn afternoon.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:14.52,0:00:17.62,English,,0,0,0,,I sat on the porch.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:17.62,0:00:23.36,English,,0,0,0,,The breeze felt pleasant, and I observed the trees in the garden swaying slowly.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:23.36,0:00:28.66,English,,0,0,0,,Grandmother made tea and had me hold the cup.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:28.66,0:00:33.08,English,,0,0,0,,She always lets me read any book I like.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:35.00,0:00:40.50,English,,0,0,0,,Today she let me rest as long as I wanted.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:40.50,0:00:44.26,English,,0,0,0,,I could see petals drift on the wind.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:45.70,0:00:51.46,English,,0,0,0,,I could hear a distant bird sing beyond the hedge.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:51.46,0:00:58.58,English,,0,0,0,,Close your eyes and allow the wind to carry you, grandmother said gently.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:00.98,0:01:07.74,English,,0,0,0,,Grandfather used to admire the plum tree in our garden.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:12.30,0:01:20.74,English,,0,0,0,,Grandmother often recalled that memory and smiles quietly.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:20.74,0:01:29.16,English,,0,0,0,,I sensed that she wanted to encourage me to remember him.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:29.16,0:01:38.16,English,,0,0,0,,Soon the evening sun painted the roof in gentle tones.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:38.16,0:01:44.08,English,,0,0,0,,The garden became calm and golden.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:46.36,0:01:50.40,English,,0,0,0,,Grandmother handed me a fresh cup.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:50.40,0:01:57.80,English,,0,0,0,,I wished she would let me stay on the porch forever.
